\[|z - 12| + |z - 5i| = |z - 12| + |5i - z| \ge |(z - 12) + (5i - z)| = |-12 + 5i| = 13.\]But we are told that $|z - 12| + |z - 5i| = 13.$  The only way that equality can occur is if $z$ lies on the line segment connecting 12 and $5i$ in the complex plane.

